00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,760
Exercise 1-24, Application of Stress. Now, read each sentence of the paragraph after

2
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:13,240
the speaker. Use your rubber band, give a clear pitch change to the marked words,

3
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:21,880
and think about the meaning that the pitch is conveying. Hello. My name is Anne. I'm

4
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:29,040
taking American accent training. There's a lot to learn. But, I hope to make it as

5
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:39,240
enjoyable as possible. I should pick up on the American intonation pattern pretty

6
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:45,100
easily, although the only way to get it is to practice all the time.

7
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:59,600
I use the up and down or peaks and valleys intonation more than I used to. I've been

8
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,820
paying attention to pitch too.

9
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:11,680
It's like walking down a staircase. I've been talking to a lot of Americans lately

10
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:16,800
and they tell me that I'm easier to understand.

11
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:28,320
Anyway, I could go on and on, but the important thing is to listen well and

12
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:37,000
sound good. Well, what do you think? Do I? Listen and make any corrections. After

13
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,280
you've put in the accent marks where you think they belong, take a highlighter, and

14
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:46,940
as I read very slowly, mark the words that I stress. I'm going to exaggerate the

15
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:51,680
words far more than you'd normally hear in a normal reading of the paragraph. You can

16
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:56,220
mark either the whole word or just the strong syllable, whichever you prefer, so

17
00:01:56,220 --> 00:02:01,440
that you have a bright spot of color for where the stress should fall. Note, if you

18
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:06,240
do the exercise only in pencil, your eye and mind will tend to skip over the accent

19
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:10,840
marks. The spots of color, however, will register as different and thereby

20
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:15,920
encourage your pitch change. This may strike you as unusual, but trust me, it

21
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:20,420
works. Practice reading the paragraph out loud three times on your own.
